  "notes": "Most commonly encountered in emergency and medical contexts to describe transporting patients or injured people to a hospital. Also used in industrial contexts for conveying materials or goods.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {緊急|きんきゅう}{搬送|はんそう}: emergency transport\n- {救急|きゅうきゅう}{搬送|はんそう}: ambulance transport\n- {病院|びょういん}に{搬送|はんそう}する: to transport to a hospital\n- {搬送|はんそう}{先|さき}: destination of transport\n- ベルトコンベヤーで{搬送|はんそう}する: to convey by belt conveyor\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {運搬|うんぱん}: transportation, hauling — broader term for transporting goods or materials\n- {輸送|ゆそう}: transport, shipping — used for larger-scale logistics and freight\n- {運|はこ}ぶ: to carry, to transport — everyday general-purpose verb",
